RC_kwDOAO6SJc7qsi55","diff_hunk":"@@ -191,6 +191,13 @@ String ResourceUID::get_id_path(ID p_id) const {\n \tconst ResourceUID::Cache *cache = unique_ids.getptr(p_id);\n \n #if TOOLS_ENABLED\n+\tif (!cache) {\n+\t\tconst ResourceUID::Cache *copy_cache = unique_ids_copy.getptr(p_id);\n+\t\tif (copy_cache) {\n+\t\t\treturn String::utf8(copy_cache->cs.ptr());\n+\t\t}\n+\t}","path":"core/io/resource_uid.cpp","commit_id":"af0b3ae7757248469b98e77a08448ebd97c92532","original_commit_id":"2358a7af19769e80d6cebb580e30d71f0d3d3089","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Alright, yeah, that would indeed be problematic.\r\n\r\nThe fragility of these different \"views\" into the UIDs is starting to worry me though, but I'm not sure how to best fix it, since they both have their use.\r\n\r\nFor example, since we don't currently have a `has_id` check in `ResourceLoader::_validate_local_path`, any resource load done using `uid://` will now potentially return a stale path if it happens to be done during the import, since it'll always go through `get_id_path` and thus `unique_ids_copy`.\r\n\r\nSo sometimes it'll be a problem if you do check `has_id` beforehand, because you'd miss existing entries, and sometimes it'll be a problem if you don't check `has_id`, because you'd get stale data.\r\n\r\nAnd these problems will of course only manifest randomly during import in non-trivial projects.\r\n\r\nI don't know, maybe I'm overthinking it, and it'll be fine.","created_at":"2026-09-04T20:05:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T20:05:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123024#discussion_r3937545849","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123024","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3937545849"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123024#discussion_r3937545849"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123024"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3937545849/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":194,"original_start_line":194,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":199,"original_line":199,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3904666898,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":9,"position":9,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3937716573","pull_request_review_id":5117569889,"id":3937716573,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7qtMld","diff_hunk":"@@ -191,6 +191,13 @@ String ResourceUID::get_id_path(ID p_id) const {\n \tconst ResourceUID::Cache *cache = unique_ids.getptr(p_id);\n \n #if TOOLS_ENABLED\n+\tif (!cache) {\n+\t\tconst ResourceUID::Cache *copy_cache = unique_ids_copy.getptr(p_id);\n+\t\tif (copy_cache) {\n+\t\t\treturn String::utf8(copy_cache->cs.ptr());\n+\t\t}\n+\t}","path":"core/io/resource_uid.cpp","commit_id":"af0b3ae7757248469b98e77a08448ebd97c92532","original_commit_id":"2358a7af19769e80d6cebb580e30d71f0d3d3089","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIy